From ee21211b378cf685deef79995c42ffad048d8560 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:58:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: stop writing lowLevelAccess into the character's saved
 triggers

runLuaEditTrigger() and runTrigger() in display mode build their trigger
lists from the character object in the save itself, and set
lowLevelAccess on each of its triggers: false in runLuaEditTrigger(),
the character's own setting in runTrigger(). Both run whenever a message
is rendered, so for a character with low level access enabled the flag
flips back and forth, the save is marked changed and written out again
in full, just from scrolling through a chat.

Build both lists from copies, as runLuaButtonTrigger() already does. The
Lua runtime gets the same lowLevelAccess value as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
